{"body":"## Context\n\n`radicle-artifact` today serves artifacts via a one-shot foreground `rad-artifact serve` (`src/share/serve.rs`) that:\n- spins up an iroh endpoint keyed to the user's radicle DID via `radicle_secret_to_iroh`\n- uses a per-PID temp `FsStore` with `ImportMode::TryReference`\n- writes a bare `iroh://` location to the COB, with the consumer deriving the endpoint id from the author DID\n\nMeanwhile `radicle-desktop` (`crates/radicle-types/src/seeder.rs`) has independently built what is effectively the seeder we want:\n- persistent `FsStore` at `<home>/artifacts/store/`\n- independent persisted iroh key at `<home>/artifacts/iroh.key`\n- `ImportMode::Copy` so source files can be moved or deleted after seeding\n- iroh-blobs **tags** (`seeded/{cid}`) as the single source of truth for \"what am I seeding\"; no sidecar index\n- explicit `iroh://{endpoint_id}` location URLs\n\nThe two implementations have drifted and the desktop's approach is the better one. This issue tracks reconciling them and unblocking a multi-tenant seeder daemon (one host seeding many users' artifacts).\n\n## Design decisions\n\n1. **Standalone seeder identity, forward-only.** All new writes use an independent persisted iroh key and explicit `iroh://{endpoint_id}` location URLs. The seeder is its own peer; the author DID just signs the COB op.\n2. **Bare `iroh://` is read-only compat.** The existing resolver branch at `src/bin/rad-artifact.rs:1215-…` that derives the endpoint id from the author DID stays as a read-side shim for already-published locations. No new code writes bare URLs.\n3. **Tags, not a sidecar file.** Use `seeded/{cid}` tags as local state, matching desktop. No `pins.json` or equivalent.\n4. **Library owns the primitives.** `Seeder`, `bootstrap`, `seed`, `unseed`, `is_seeded`, `seeded_cids`, `artifact_size` live in `radicle-artifact`. Frontends (CLI, desktop, future daemon) are thin callers. The library knows about blobs/store/tags; it does **not** know about COBs — the caller composes `seed()` + `add_location()`.\n\n## Plan\n\n### 1. Hoist `Seeder` into `radicle-artifact`\n\nAdd a `radicle_artifact::seeder` module containing the primitives currently in `radicle-desktop/crates/radicle-types/src/seeder.rs`:\n- `Seeder { blobs, router }`\n- `bootstrap(home: &Path) -> Result<Seeder>`\n- `import_blob`, `import_collection` (both `ImportMode::Copy`)\n- `register_seeded`, `unregister_seeded`, `is_seeded` (tag-based)\n- `seed`, `unseed`, `is_seeded_str` (string wrappers for CID-crate-free callers)\n- `seeded_cids`, `artifact_size`, `artifact_size_str`\n- `our_iroh_url(endpoint) -> String` returning `iroh://{endpoint_id}`\n\n### 2. Switch `rad-artifact serve` to standalone identity\n\nIn `src/bin/rad-artifact.rs::run_serve`:\n- Replace `radicle_secret_to_iroh(...)` + temp `FsStore` with `seeder::bootstrap(home)`\n- Replace `add_blob`/`add_collection` from `share::serve` with `seeder::seed`\n- Write the location as `seeder::our_iroh_url(endpoint)` (explicit) instead of bare `iroh://`\n- On Ctrl-C, retract the explicit URL but leave the seeded tag in place — the seeded set is persistent intent, not tied to one process\n\n### 3. Normalize URL forms in the consumer\n\nIn `artifact_locations` (`src/bin/rad-artifact.rs:1215-…`):\n- When resolving locations, canonicalize bare `iroh://` (derived from author DID) and explicit `iroh://{id}` to the same key when the ids match, so they dedupe during the transition\n- Comment the bare-URL branch as a read-only compat shim with a sunset note\n\n### 4. Cut `radicle-desktop` over to the library\n\nIn `radicle-desktop`:\n- Delete `crates/radicle-types/src/seeder.rs`\n- Call into `radicle_artifact::seeder` from the Tauri command layer (`crates/radicle-tauri/src/commands/cob/release.rs`)\n- Tauri commands stay as the COB-aware composition layer (seed-then-`AddLocation`)\n\nThis is the proof the abstraction sits in the right place; should be a near-pure rename + dep bump.\n\n### 5. Daemon binary (follow-up, separate issue)\n\nOnce 1–4 land, the standalone seeder daemon is essentially \"the library + a Unix socket exposing the same verbs the Tauri commands already expose.\" Sketch of the shape:\n\n- **Process**: a small binary (`rad-artifact-node`, or folded in as `rad-artifact daemon start`) that calls `seeder::bootstrap(home)` once at startup and runs until stopped. One process, one endpoint, many seeded CIDs.\n- **Layout**: reuses the library's `<home>/artifacts/{store/, iroh.key}` exactly as desktop already lays it out. Adds a Unix socket at `$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/rad-artifact/daemon.sock` (0600) and a pid/endpoint-id file for cheap `status` lookups.\n- **Control protocol**: newline-delimited JSON over the socket, one request/response per connection. Verbs mirror the Tauri commands — `seed`, `unseed`, `is_seeding`, `list_seeded`, plus `status` and `shutdown`. Auth is file permissions; no network exposure.\n- **COB writes**: the daemon stays out of the COB. `seed`/`unseed` on the socket import/untag bytes and return the endpoint URL; the *client* composes that with an `AddLocation`/`RemoveLocation` op signed by the user's radicle key. Keeps the daemon's identity (the iroh key) and the author's identity (the radicle DID) cleanly separate, and avoids the daemon needing keystore access.\n- **CLI integration**: `rad-artifact serve <PATH>` auto-detects the socket — if present, send `seed` + write the location and exit immediately (no foreground Ctrl-C dance); if absent, fall back to today's foreground behavior. Adds a small `rad-artifact daemon {start,status,stop,list,unseed}` surface for management.\n\nTracked separately to keep this issue focused on the reconciliation.\n\n## Migration notes\n\n- Users with previously-published bare `iroh://` locations stay discoverable: the consumer-side derivation still resolves them. Their old radicle-derived endpoint is reachable as long as the old binary is running.\n- After upgrading and re-seeding, a new explicit `iroh://{id}` location is written. The old bare location remains in the COB pointing at an endpoint that is no longer listening; other locations cover for it, or the user explicitly retracts it.\n- `radicle_secret_to_iroh` can stay as dead code for one release for migration tooling, then be removed.\n\n## README / docs\n\nAdd a short paragraph distinguishing the two identities:\n- Your **radicle DID** signs COB ops (including `AddLocation`).\n- Your **seeder** has its own persisted iroh key; locations are announced by explicit endpoint id.\n\nThe README line that frames the DID as \"1:1 with NodeID\" is still true for COB signing, but no longer governs serving.\n\n## What we deliberately lose\n\nThe \"iroh endpoint id == author's DID\" cryptographic shortcut goes away. Trust already lives in the CID rather than the endpoint identity (anyone can announce a location for any CID), so this is an honest framing change rather than a security regression.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `radicle_artifact::seeder` module exists with the primitives listed in step 1.\n- [ ] `rad-artifact serve` uses standalone identity and writes explicit `iroh://{id}` URLs.\n- [ ] Consumer-side resolution dedupes bare and explicit URL forms when they refer to the same endpoint.\n- [ ] `radicle-desktop`'s `seeder.rs` is deleted in favour of the library.\n- [ ] Existing bare-`iroh://` locations published by old `rad-artifact` versions remain fetchable.\n- [ ] README distinguishes COB-signing identity from seeder identity.\n- [ ] `cargo fmt` and `cargo clippy` clean.","type":"comment"}